-- Slow news days and Sean's tips (Sean, 2026-10-31). Central Florida's Pulse had no stories on 18 of 20 days while
-- unused Vegan stories sat in the pool: "if it's vegan and it's a slow news day, let's pull those in... it's better
-- than having nothing." And: "I want to be able to screenshot it, grab a link, voice dictate it... you should be able
-- to take that, do some additional research, and then put it in the queue." The writer now fills a thin briefing from
-- older unused Vegan stories and the national pool, and reads the team's tips (HQ Depot > Send a story: origin 'link',
-- reason starting "Tip") first, researching each before using it.
update public.lesaruss_dispatch_sources set instructions =
  replace(instructions,
    'If there is not enough real news, a shorter briefing (even one story or none) with a strong event or action is better than padding.',
    'If there is not enough real news, follow Slow news days below: an older Vegan story is better than none, but never pad with fluff.')
  || E'\n\nSlow news days (Sean, 2026-10-31: "if it''s vegan and it''s a slow news day, let''s pull those in... it''s better than having nothing"). Every city briefing carries at least 3 stories whenever Vegan news exists. If step 3a gives fewer than 3 usable city stories, run it again with interval ''45 days'' instead of 7 (still unused, still the city), and for washington-dc, maryland and virginia also read city_slug = ''dmv'' (the old shared chapter; use a dmv story only in the place it is really about). Skip anything that has passed (an event that is over, a deal that ended). Then fill to at least 3 with step 3d''s national stories, widening 3d to interval ''14 days'' if needed. Say when a story is more than a week old ("Earlier this month..."), never present it as today''s news. A briefing with no stories is only for a week with no Vegan news anywhere.\n\nTips from the team (Sean, 2026-10-31). Sean and the team send stories from HQ Depot > Send a story: a link, a screenshot, or what someone told them, spoken or typed. They are ve_news_leads rows with origin = ''link'' and a reason starting with "Tip"; sean_note holds their words and image_url the screenshot. Read them first in step 3a (for the city, or city_slug null for any city they fit), last 14 days, unused:\n   select id, title, url, summary, sean_note, image_url, city_slug, created_at from ve_news_leads where brand_slug = ''vegans-explore'' and origin = ''link'' and status = ''new'' and topic_post_id is null and created_at > now() - interval ''14 days'' and (city_slug = ''<city>'' or city_slug is null) order by created_at desc;\n   A tip is a lead, never a source: WebSearch it, WebFetch the original (the outlet''s article, the business''s own post or page), and use only what a real source says, with that source''s url. A tip you cannot confirm is left for the next run, never published on the team''s word alone. A confirmed tip leads the briefing ahead of feed stories. Never name who sent it.',
  notes = coalesce(notes, '') || E'\n2026-10-31: Slow news days (at least 3 stories, widen to 45 days and the national pool) and Tips from the team (Sean).'
where key = 'pulse_topic_write' and instructions not like '%Slow news days (Sean, 2026-10-31%';
